WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.237
Time: 3 minutes.

00:00:01.477 --> 00:00:03.739
Avery resubmits TS-104.

00:00:03.979 --> 00:00:07.563
Do not assume a correction request guarantees a correct result.

00:00:07.803 --> 00:00:15.589
Reopen the relevant record, confirm the period and assignment, and repeat the comparison for changed lines and the overall total.

00:00:16.279 --> 00:00:22.679
The corrected packet shows 8 DEL, 8 DEL, 6 DEL + 2 TRN, 8 DEL, and 6 DEL.

00:00:22.919 --> 00:00:24.114
Total: 38.

00:00:24.354 --> 00:00:30.583
All supporting evidence now agrees and no unresolved exception remains under the sample policy.

00:00:30.823 --> 00:00:32.743
Choose approval in the simulation.

00:00:33.433 --> 00:00:38.639
After a decision, inspect the displayed status and available history or confirmation.

00:00:38.879 --> 00:00:42.697
A click is an attempt, not proof that the intended state was reached.

00:00:42.937 --> 00:00:47.695
Approval routing is configured by the buyer and may require additional approvers.

00:00:47.935 --> 00:00:51.519
Your approval does not itself prove that an invoice has been paid.

00:00:52.209 --> 00:01:00.059
Worked handoff: ‘Supervisor review completed for TS-104, 5–9 October: 38 hours verified.

00:01:00.299 --> 00:01:05.547
System shows the next approval stage.’ This is accurate if that is what the record displays.

00:01:05.787 --> 00:01:11.547
Avoid saying ‘payment completed’ unless a separate authorized payment record actually supports it.

00:01:11.787 --> 00:01:18.977
If an error message appears, inspect the current record before retrying to avoid a duplicate or contradictory action.

00:01:19.667 --> 00:01:20.755
Now it's your turn.

00:01:20.995 --> 00:01:24.664
After your approval, the screen indicates another approval stage.

00:01:24.904 --> 00:01:26.035
What do you report?

00:01:26.275 --> 00:01:29.389
